From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:09:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(blocks): apply native fence geometry in Bedrock sessions

Adapt core Bedrock 1.26.51 fence bounds to Java collision, selection and
camera hooks. Preserve float world rounding before rebasing and use
separate physical arms instead of the rectangular outline envelope.
Accepted versioned server-pack metadata enables the same hooks through
ViaProxy; ordinary Java sessions retain their existing shapes.

The pinned native executable establishes geometry for supplied connection
bits. Connectivity production, ordered movement resolution and the
rendered fence mesh remain separate work.
